    "updated_at": "2021-08-06T19:03:16Z",
    "body": "It turns out Chromium and WebKit distinguish between user-triggered reloads and other reloads. Test case:\r\n\r\n- Go to https://example.com/\r\n- Click the \"more information\" link taking you to https://www.iana.org/domains/reserved\r\n- Open your console and type `document.referrer`. You get `https://example.com/`\r\n- Press the reload button on your browser\r\n- Open your console and type `document.referrer`. You get `https://example.com/`\r\n- In the same console, type `location.reload()`.\r\n- Open your console and type `document.referrer`. You get:\r\n   - `https://example.com/` in Firefox\r\n   - `https://www.iana.org/domains/reserved` in Chromium, due to [this code](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/loader/frame_loader.cc;l=163;drc=23289e8c2e72bb6c996dd012dbb74d1beeecc5dc;bpv=1;bpt=1)\r\n   - `https://www.iana.org/domains/reserved` in WebKit",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
